CD32 MPEG device presence regression
===================================

Build with test-devices-cd32mpeg-presence or its -quick target. The native
Amiga MPEG component group selects both normal and quick targets.

Run mpegpresence on a stock CD32 with 2 MiB Chip RAM, then with an FMV
cartridge fitted. It checks FindResident(), the initialized device list,
and the return code of the actual Version command used by game scripts.
The first argument optionally supplies a Version executable path instead
of C:Version, for minimal test boot volumes.

Expected: 4/4 checks pass in each configuration. Without a cartridge the
resident and device are absent, and Version returns WARN or greater. With
a cartridge both are present, and Version succeeds.
